IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `niis-dates`

-- National Injury Insurance Scheme (Queensland) Act 2016 -- the scheme as a seriously injured person meets it,
-- seat-neutral core.
--
-- In the Act's own actors and terms: "the injured person", "the applicant", "the participant", "the agency" (the
-- National Injury Insurance Agency, Queensland), "the insurer", "the court", "the medical tribunal", "QCAT". The injured
-- person's questions are in niis-seat.l4; this module holds the rules.
--
-- Edition: National Injury Insurance Scheme (Queensland) Act 2016 (act-2016-034), the version in force from 1 July
-- 2024, current on 6 November 2026, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/act-2016-034.txt. The National
-- Injury Insurance Scheme (Queensland) Regulation 2016, which sets the eligibility criteria (s 12(1)(b)), the buy-in
-- injuries and contribution (s 13), the payment caps (s 37(5)(a)) and the s 17(4) waiting period, is not deposited:
-- each is asked as a fact.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `National Injury Insurance Scheme (Queensland) Act 2016`

§§ `Schedule 1 -- serious personal injury`

-- Schedule 1: "serious personal injury means a personal injury that is-- (a) a permanent spinal cord injury resulting
-- in a permanent neurological deficit; or (b) a traumatic brain injury resulting in a permanent impairment of
-- cognitive, physical or psychosocial function; or (c) a forequarter amputation or shoulder disarticulation amputation;
-- or (d) the amputation of a leg through or above the femur; or (e) the amputation of more than 1 limb or parts of
-- different limbs; or (f) a permanent injury to the brachial plexus resulting in an impairment equivalent to a shoulder
-- disarticulation amputation; or (g) a full thickness burn to all or part of the body; or (h) an inhalation burn
-- resulting in a permanent respiratory impairment; or (i) permanent blindness caused by a trauma."
DECLARE `Injury` IS ONE OF
    `a permanent spinal cord injury resulting in a permanent neurological deficit`
    `a traumatic brain injury resulting in a permanent impairment of cognitive, physical or psychosocial function`
    `a forequarter amputation or shoulder disarticulation amputation`
    `the amputation of a leg through or above the femur`
    `the amputation of more than 1 limb or parts of different limbs`
    `a permanent injury to the brachial plexus resulting in an impairment equivalent to a shoulder disarticulation amputation`
    `a full thickness burn to all or part of the body`
    `an inhalation burn resulting in a permanent respiratory impairment`
    `permanent blindness caused by a trauma`
    `another personal injury`

-- "means": the list is closed, so another injury is not a serious personal injury.
GIVEN `the injury` IS AN `Injury`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a serious personal injury` `the injury` IF
    CONSIDER `the injury`
    WHEN `another personal injury` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `ss 4 and 7 -- when the Act applies`

-- s 7: "A prescribed vehicle is-- (a) a motor vehicle or a trailer for which a CTP insurance policy is in force; or (b)
-- a trailer to which a CTP insurance policy extends; or (c) a motor vehicle of which a self-insurer is the registered
-- owner; or (d) a trailer for which a self-insurer would be the insurer ...; or (e) a motor vehicle or a trailer to
-- which a nominal defendant scheme would apply ..."
-- s 4(4): "uninsured motor vehicle means a prescribed vehicle-- (a) for which a CTP insurance policy is not in force;
-- and (b) of which a self-insurer is not the registered owner; and (c) that is not a trailer."
-- The vehicle is described by the person in one of these ways. An unidentified vehicle is one the person cannot say
-- was uninsured (a fork line in NOTES.md).
DECLARE `Vehicle` IS ONE OF
    `a motor vehicle with a CTP insurance policy in force`
    `a trailer with a CTP insurance policy in force, or to which one extends`
    `a motor vehicle whose registered owner is a self-insurer`
    `a trailer for which a self-insurer would be the insurer`
    `an uninsured motor vehicle to which a nominal defendant scheme applies`
    `an uninsured trailer to which a nominal defendant scheme applies`
    `an unidentified motor vehicle or trailer to which a nominal defendant scheme applies`
    `a vehicle that is none of these`

GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A `Vehicle`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a prescribed vehicle (s 7)` `the vehicle` IF
    CONSIDER `the vehicle`
    WHEN `a vehicle that is none of these` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A `Vehicle`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an uninsured motor vehicle (s 4(4))` `the vehicle` IF
    CONSIDER `the vehicle`
    WHEN `an uninsured motor vehicle to which a nominal defendant scheme applies` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 4(1)(a): the injury "is a result of-- (i) the driving of the prescribed vehicle; or (ii) a collision, or action
-- taken to avoid a collision, with the prescribed vehicle; or (iii) the prescribed vehicle running out of control; or
-- (iv) a defect in the prescribed vehicle causing loss of control of the vehicle while the vehicle is being driven".
DECLARE `How the injury happened` IS ONE OF
    `the driving of the vehicle`
    `a collision, or action taken to avoid a collision, with the vehicle`
    `the vehicle running out of control`
    `a defect in the vehicle causing loss of control while it was being driven`
    `some other way`

-- s 4(3)(a): the vehicles that count only on a road.
DECLARE `Kind of vehicle` IS ONE OF
    `a tractor, backhoe, bulldozer, end-loader, forklift, industrial crane or hoist, or other mobile machinery`
    `an agricultural machine being used for agricultural purposes`
    `a motor vehicle adapted to run on rail or tram tracks`
    `an amphibious vehicle`
    `a motor vehicle prescribed by regulation under s 4(3)(a)(v)`
    `an ordinary vehicle`

DECLARE `Where it happened` IS ONE OF
    `on a road`
    `in a public place that is not a road`
    `somewhere else`

DECLARE `Application of the Act` IS ONE OF
    `the Act applies to the injury`
    `no: the injury is not a serious personal injury`
    `no: no prescribed vehicle was involved (s 7)`
    `no: the injury did not result from the vehicle in a way s 4(1)(a) lists`
    `no: the motor accident did not happen in Queensland on or after 1 July 2016 (s 4(1)(b))`
    `no: an uninsured motor vehicle, and the accident was not on a road or in a public place (s 4(2))`
    `no: a vehicle of a kind in s 4(3)(a), and the accident was not on a road`
    `no: the vehicle was being used for an act of terrorism (s 4(3)(b))`

-- s 4(1): "This Act applies in relation to a serious personal injury caused by, through or in connection with a
-- prescribed vehicle, if-- (a) [the four ways]; and (b) the incident (the motor accident) resulting in the injury
-- happens in Queensland on or after 1 July 2016." (2): "However, this Act does not apply ... [to] an uninsured motor
-- vehicle, other than a prescribed vehicle stated in subsection (3)(a), unless the motor accident ... happens on a road
-- or public place." (3): "Also, this Act does not apply ... [to] (a) [the s 4(3)(a) vehicles] unless the motor accident
-- ... happens on a road ...; or (b) a prescribed vehicle that ... is being used for the actual doing of an act or
-- making of a threat that is an act of terrorism." "Road", "public place" and "act of terrorism" are borrowed terms,
-- asked as facts. Every "no" here is the text's own ("if", "does not apply").
GIVEN `the injury`                        IS AN `Injury`
      `the vehicle`                       IS A `Vehicle`
      `how it happened`                   IS A `How the injury happened`
      `the kind of vehicle`               IS A `Kind of vehicle`
      `where it happened`                 IS A `Where it happened`
      `it happened in Queensland`         IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the motor accident`     IS A DATE
      `the vehicle was used for terrorism` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Application of the Act`
`the s 4 answer` `the injury` `the vehicle` `how it happened` `the kind of vehicle` `where it happened` `it happened in Queensland` `the day of the motor accident` `the vehicle was used for terrorism` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`is a serious personal injury` `the injury`)
            THEN `no: the injury is not a serious personal injury`
        IF NOT (`is a prescribed vehicle (s 7)` `the vehicle`)
            THEN `no: no prescribed vehicle was involved (s 7)`
        IF `how it happened` EQUALS `some other way`
            THEN `no: the injury did not result from the vehicle in a way s 4(1)(a) lists`
        IF NOT (`it happened in Queensland` AND ((DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2016) `is no later than` `the day of the motor accident`))
            THEN `no: the motor accident did not happen in Queensland on or after 1 July 2016 (s 4(1)(b))`
        IF `a s 4(3)(a) vehicle` AND (NOT (`where it happened` EQUALS `on a road`))
            THEN `no: a vehicle of a kind in s 4(3)(a), and the accident was not on a road`
        IF (NOT `a s 4(3)(a) vehicle`) AND (`is an uninsured motor vehicle (s 4(4))` `the vehicle`) AND (`where it happened` EQUALS `somewhere else`)
            THEN `no: an uninsured motor vehicle, and the accident was not on a road or in a public place (s 4(2))`
        IF `the vehicle was used for terrorism`
            THEN `no: the vehicle was being used for an act of terrorism (s 4(3)(b))`
        OTHERWISE `the Act applies to the injury`
    WHERE
        `a s 4(3)(a) vehicle` MEANS NOT (`the kind of vehicle` EQUALS `an ordinary vehicle`)

§§ `s 12 -- eligibility`

DECLARE `Eligibility` IS ONE OF
    `eligible to participate in the scheme (s 12)`
    `not eligible: the Act does not apply to the injury (s 12(1)(a))`
    `not eligible: the injury does not meet the eligibility criteria prescribed by regulation (s 12(1)(b))`
    `not eligible: damages for treatment, care and support needs were awarded and paid other than by the agency under s 44(3)(a) (s 12(2))`
    `not eligible: the injury did not permanently increase a disability the person already had (s 12(3))`

-- s 12(1): "A person is eligible to participate in the scheme in relation to a serious personal injury ... if-- (a)
-- this Act applies in relation to the injury; and (b) the injury meets the criteria (the eligibility criteria) for the
-- injury prescribed by regulation." (2): "However, a person is not eligible ... if-- (a) the person has been awarded
-- damages, under a final judgment of a court or a binding settlement, in relation to the person's treatment, care and
-- support needs as a result of the injury; and (b) the damages were paid other than by way of a payment by the agency
-- under section 44(3)(a)." (3): "Also, a person is not eligible ... if-- (a) before the motor accident ... the person
-- suffered from another injury or condition; and (b) the serious personal injury does not permanently increase the
-- extent of any disability experienced by the person before the motor accident."
-- The eligibility criteria are in the regulation (not deposited): whether the injury meets them is a fact, and in
-- practice the agency's decision (reviewable by the medical tribunal, s 112(1)(b)).
GIVEN `the Act applies`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury meets the eligibility criteria`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `damages for the needs were awarded`              IS A BOOLEAN
      `those damages were paid other than under s 44(3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had another injury or condition before the accident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury permanently increased the earlier disability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Eligibility`
`the s 12 answer` `the Act applies` `the injury meets the eligibility criteria` `damages for the needs were awarded` `those damages were paid other than under s 44(3)(a)` `the person had another injury or condition before the accident` `the injury permanently increased the earlier disability` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Act applies`
            THEN `not eligible: the Act does not apply to the injury (s 12(1)(a))`
        IF NOT `the injury meets the eligibility criteria`
            THEN `not eligible: the injury does not meet the eligibility criteria prescribed by regulation (s 12(1)(b))`
        IF `damages for the needs were awarded` AND `those damages were paid other than under s 44(3)(a)`
            THEN `not eligible: damages for treatment, care and support needs were awarded and paid other than by the agency under s 44(3)(a) (s 12(2))`
        IF `the person had another injury or condition before the accident` AND (NOT `the injury permanently increased the earlier disability`)
            THEN `not eligible: the injury did not permanently increase a disability the person already had (s 12(3))`
        OTHERWISE `eligible to participate in the scheme (s 12)`

§§ `s 13 -- buying into the scheme`

DECLARE `Buy-in` IS ONE OF
    `s 13 does not apply: the person is eligible under s 12, and applies under s 16`
    `s 13 does not apply: the injury is not one prescribed by regulation for buying in`
    `the agency may accept the person as a buy-in participant for an agreed period; the contribution must then be paid within 28 days (s 13(2)-(4))`

-- s 13(1): "This section applies to a person who-- (a) suffers a serious personal injury prescribed by regulation; and
-- (b) is not eligible under section 12 ..." (2): "The agency may decide to accept the person ... for a period agreed
-- between the person and the agency." (3)-(4): the contribution, "calculated in the way prescribed by regulation"; "If
-- the contribution is not paid within 28 days after the person is accepted as a participant, the person-- (a) stops
-- being a participant; and (b) is taken to have never been a participant."
GIVEN `the person is eligible under s 12`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury is prescribed for buying in`  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Buy-in`
`the s 13 answer` `the person is eligible under s 12` `the injury is prescribed for buying in` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is eligible under s 12`
            THEN `s 13 does not apply: the person is eligible under s 12, and applies under s 16`
        IF NOT `the injury is prescribed for buying in`
            THEN `s 13 does not apply: the injury is not one prescribed by regulation for buying in`
        OTHERWISE `the agency may accept the person as a buy-in participant for an agreed period; the contribution must then be paid within 28 days (s 13(2)-(4))`

GIVEN `the day accepted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to pay the buy-in contribution (s 13(4))` `the day accepted` MEANS `the day` 28 `days after` `the day accepted`

DECLARE `Buy-in standing` IS ONE OF
    `a buy-in participant: the contribution was paid in time`
    `a buy-in participant for now; the contribution must be paid by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `no longer a participant, and taken never to have been one (s 13(4))`

GIVEN `the day accepted`          IS A DATE
      `the contribution was paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was paid`       IS A DATE
      `today`                     IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Buy-in standing`
`the s 13(4) answer` `the day accepted` `the contribution was paid` `the day it was paid` `today` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the contribution was paid` AND `the day it was paid` `is no later than` `the last day`
            THEN `a buy-in participant: the contribution was paid in time`
        IF `today` `is no later than` `the last day`
            THEN `a buy-in participant for now; the contribution must be paid by` `the last day`
        OTHERWISE `no longer a participant, and taken never to have been one (s 13(4))`
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS `the last day to pay the buy-in contribution (s 13(4))` `the day accepted`

§§ `ss 16-18 -- applying`

-- s 16(2): "If the application is made within 1 year after the motor accident happened (the application period), the
-- agency must accept the application." (3): after it, "the agency must decide whether or not to accept the
-- application", considering whether it would be fair and reasonable (s 16(4)). To "accept the application" is to take
-- it for decision, not to accept the person into the scheme (s 22 decides that).
GIVEN `the day of the motor accident` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the application period (s 16(2))` `the day of the motor accident` MEANS
    `the day` 1 `years after` `the day of the motor accident`

DECLARE `Acceptance of the application` IS ONE OF
    `the agency must accept the application (s 16(2))`
    `the application is late: the agency decides whether it is fair and reasonable to accept it (s 16(3)-(4))`
    `s 16(2) and (3) do not apply after a s 44(3)(a) payment (s 17(4)(b)); even if the injured person is eligible, the agency may refuse unless it is satisfied of severe financial hardship (s 22(4)-(5))`

GIVEN `the day of the motor accident`         IS A DATE
      `the day the application is made`       IS A DATE
      `a s 44(3)(a) payment has been received` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Acceptance of the application`
`the s 16 answer` `the day of the motor accident` `the day the application is made` `a s 44(3)(a) payment has been received` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a s 44(3)(a) payment has been received`
            THEN `s 16(2) and (3) do not apply after a s 44(3)(a) payment (s 17(4)(b)); even if the injured person is eligible, the agency may refuse unless it is satisfied of severe financial hardship (s 22(4)-(5))`
        IF `the day the application is made` `is no later than` (`the last day of the application period (s 16(2))` `the day of the motor accident`)
            THEN `the agency must accept the application (s 16(2))`
        OTHERWISE `the application is late: the agency decides whether it is fair and reasonable to accept it (s 16(3)-(4))`

DECLARE `May apply` IS ONE OF
    `an application may be made`
    `no: another application for the injury has not been decided (s 17(1)(a))`
    `no: the injured person is already an interim participant for the injury (s 17(1)(b))`
    `no: after a refusal, or after interim participation ended, only with new medical information or information showing deterioration (s 17(3))`
    `no: after a s 44(3)(a) payment, only in the circumstances prescribed by regulation (s 17(4)(a)(i))`
    `not yet: after a s 44(3)(a) payment, an application may be made from` HAS `the first day` IS A DATE
    `an application may be made, but after a s 44(3)(a) payment the agency may refuse it even if the injured person is eligible, unless it is satisfied of severe financial hardship (s 22(4)-(5))`

-- s 17(1): "An application may not be made ... if-- (a) another person has made an application in relation to the
-- injury and the application has not been decided; or (b) the injured person is an interim participant ..." (2)-(3):
-- after a refusal, or after an interim participant's participation has ended, "A person may not make an application
-- ... unless-- (a) the person gives the agency medical information, not previously considered ... or (b) ... medical
-- information showing that the injured person's condition ... has deteriorated ..." (4): after a s 44(3)(a) payment,
-- an application "(i) may be made only in the circumstances prescribed by regulation; and (ii) may not be made for a
-- period, of at least 5 years after the payment is received, prescribed by regulation".
-- The regulation is not deposited: the prescribed period is asked in whole years, and a figure under 5 is raised to
-- the Act's floor of 5. The period of N years after the day of payment ends on the Nth anniversary; the application
-- may be made from the day after.
GIVEN `another application is undecided`                    IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injured person is an interim participant`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `an earlier application was refused or interim participation ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `new or deterioration medical information is given`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `a s 44(3)(a) payment has been received`              IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the payment was received`                    IS A DATE
      `the years prescribed after a payment`                IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed circumstances apply`                  IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the application`                          IS A DATE
GIVETH A `May apply`
`the s 17 answer` `another application is undecided` `the injured person is an interim participant` `an earlier application was refused or interim participation ended` `new or deterioration medical information is given` `a s 44(3)(a) payment has been received` `the day the payment was received` `the years prescribed after a payment` `the prescribed circumstances apply` `the day of the application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `another application is undecided`
            THEN `no: another application for the injury has not been decided (s 17(1)(a))`
        IF `the injured person is an interim participant`
            THEN `no: the injured person is already an interim participant for the injury (s 17(1)(b))`
        IF `an earlier application was refused or interim participation ended` AND (NOT `new or deterioration medical information is given`)
            THEN `no: after a refusal, or after interim participation ended, only with new medical information or information showing deterioration (s 17(3))`
        IF `a s 44(3)(a) payment has been received` AND (NOT `the prescribed circumstances apply`)
            THEN `no: after a s 44(3)(a) payment, only in the circumstances prescribed by regulation (s 17(4)(a)(i))`
        IF `a s 44(3)(a) payment has been received` AND (NOT (`the first day after the waiting period` `is no later than` `the day of the application`))
            THEN `not yet: after a s 44(3)(a) payment, an application may be made from` `the first day after the waiting period`
        IF `a s 44(3)(a) payment has been received`
            THEN `an application may be made, but after a s 44(3)(a) payment the agency may refuse it even if the injured person is eligible, unless it is satisfied of severe financial hardship (s 22(4)-(5))`
        OTHERWISE `an application may be made`
    WHERE
        `the first day after the waiting period` MEANS
            `the day` 1 `days after` (`the day` (`the larger of` `the years prescribed after a payment` `and` 5) `years after` `the day the payment was received`)

DECLARE `Who applies` IS ONE OF
    `the injured person`
    `an insurer against whom a claim for the injury has been made`
    `a parent or guardian of the injured person`
    `another person`

-- s 16(1): the injured person may apply. s 18(1): "An application may be made for an injured person-- (a) by an
-- insurer against whom a claim has been made, if the claim-- (i) relates to the injured person's serious personal
-- injury; and (ii) has not been finalised; or (b) if the injured person is a child--by the child's parent or guardian;
-- or (c) by another person who is acting for the injured person." (2): an insurer that applies must give the person a
-- copy. JUST FALSE for an insurer whose claim is finalised ("if"); for anyone else not acting for the person, NOTHING:
-- s 18 does not close its list with "only" (a fork line in NOTES.md).
GIVEN `who`                               IS A `Who applies`
      `the claim has been finalised (s 10)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injured person is a child`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts for the injured person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`may apply under ss 16 and 18` `who` `the claim has been finalised (s 10)` `the injured person is a child` `the person acts for the injured person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `the injured person` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an insurer against whom a claim for the injury has been made` THEN JUST (NOT `the claim has been finalised (s 10)`)
    WHEN `a parent or guardian of the injured person` THEN
        IF `the injured person is a child` OR `the person acts for the injured person` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `another person` THEN
        IF `the person acts for the injured person` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- s 10: "a claim against an insurer is finalised if-- (a) the claim has been settled by agreement and, if the agreement
-- must ... be sanctioned by a court or the public trustee, the sanction has been given; or (b) final judgment has been
-- given ... and, if an award of damages under the final judgment must ... be sanctioned ..., the sanction has been
-- given."
GIVEN `settled by agreement`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `final judgment given`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `a sanction is needed`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sanction is given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim is finalised (s 10)` `settled by agreement` `final judgment given` `a sanction is needed` `the sanction is given` IF
        (`settled by agreement` OR `final judgment given`)
    AND ((NOT `a sanction is needed`) OR `the sanction is given`)

§§ `ss 22-23 -- deciding an application`

DECLARE `Application decision` IS ONE OF
    `the agency must refuse the application, by an information notice (ss 22(1)(b), 23(2))`
    `the agency must accept the injured person as a participant for the participation period (s 22(1)(a))`
    `the agency must accept the injured person as a participant, for the participation period or, if it chooses, for life (s 22(1)(a), (2)-(3))`
    `the agency may refuse even though the injured person is eligible; an acceptance may be on conditions, and a refusal or conditions come by an information notice (ss 22(4)-(6), 23(2))`

-- s 22(1): "After receiving an application, the agency must-- (a) if the injured person is eligible to participate in
-- the scheme in relation to the serious personal injury--accept the person as a participant in the scheme in relation
-- to the injury for the participation period; or (b) otherwise--refuse the application." (2)-(3): if "the agency is
-- satisfied that the serious personal injury is likely to continue to meet the eligibility criteria for the injury
-- after the participation period ends", it "may, instead of accepting the injured person as a participant for the
-- participation period, accept the injured person as a participant in the scheme for the rest of the person's life".
-- (4): "Subsections (5) and (6) apply if-- (a) the injured person, or a person acting for the injured person, has
-- received a payment from the agency under section 44(3)(a) ...; and (b) the agency is not satisfied that the injured
-- person is suffering severe financial hardship." (5): "Despite subsection (1)(a), the agency may refuse the
-- application." (6): "If the agency decides to accept ..., the acceptance may be subject to conditions."
-- s 23(1)-(2): notice of the decision goes to the applicant, the injured person and any insurer with an unfinalised
-- claim; "If the agency refuses the application, or accepts the injured person on conditions, the notice must be an
-- information notice." The agency's satisfaction (ss 22(2), 22(4)(b)) is asked as a fact. Conditions are possible only
-- where s 22(4) applies, since (6) is one of the subsections (4) switches on.
GIVEN `the injured person is eligible`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agency is satisfied the injury is likely to continue to meet the criteria` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a s 44(3)(a) payment has been received`                               IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agency is satisfied of severe financial hardship`                 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Application decision`
`the s 22 answer` `the injured person is eligible` `the agency is satisfied the injury is likely to continue to meet the criteria` `a s 44(3)(a) payment has been received` `the agency is satisfied of severe financial hardship` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the injured person is eligible`)
            THEN `the agency must refuse the application, by an information notice (ss 22(1)(b), 23(2))`
        IF `a s 44(3)(a) payment has been received` AND (NOT `the agency is satisfied of severe financial hardship`)
            THEN `the agency may refuse even though the injured person is eligible; an acceptance may be on conditions, and a refusal or conditions come by an information notice (ss 22(4)-(6), 23(2))`
        IF `the agency is satisfied the injury is likely to continue to meet the criteria`
            THEN `the agency must accept the injured person as a participant, for the participation period or, if it chooses, for life (s 22(1)(a), (2)-(3))`
        OTHERWISE `the agency must accept the injured person as a participant for the participation period (s 22(1)(a))`

§§ `ss 21-24, 29, 31-32, 36-39 and schedule 1 -- the decision-making period`

DECLARE `Request kind` IS ONE OF
    `an application to participate (ss 16, 22)`
    `a service request (ss 28, 31)`
    `a payment request (ss 35, 37)`

-- Schedule 1: "decision-making period, for an application, service request or payment request, means-- (a) if an
-- information request is made ...--the period of 28 days after the further information requested is given to the
-- agency; or (b) otherwise--the period of 28 days after the agency receives the application, service request or payment
-- request." An information request "must be made within 28 days after" the application or request is received (ss
-- 21(2), 29(2), 36(2)(a)); one made later is read as not an information request, so (b) applies (a fork line). s 22(8):
-- for an application only, the agency may by notice extend the period "by not more than 28 days" (an extension above
-- 28 is cut to 28). s 24(3): the period includes the extension.
-- NOTHING: an information request was made in time and the information has not yet been given, so the period has not
-- started.
GIVEN `the kind`                                 IS A `Request kind`
      `the day the agency received it`           IS A DATE
      `an information request was made`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the information request`       IS A DATE
      `the information has been given`           IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the information was given`        IS A DATE
      `the days of extension`                    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day of the decision-making period` `the kind` `the day the agency received it` `an information request was made` `the day of the information request` `the information has been given` `the day the information was given` `the days of extension` MEANS
    IF `a timely information request`
    THEN IF `the information has been given`
         THEN JUST (`the day` (28 PLUS `the extension`) `days after` `the day the information was given`)
         ELSE NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the day` (28 PLUS `the extension`) `days after` `the day the agency received it`)
    WHERE
        `a timely information request` MEANS
                `an information request was made`
            AND `the day of the information request` `is no later than` (`the day` 28 `days after` `the day the agency received it`)
        `the extension` MEANS
            IF `the kind` EQUALS `an application to participate (ss 16, 22)`
            THEN `the larger of` 0 `and` (`the smaller of` `the days of extension` `and` 28)
            ELSE 0

DECLARE `Decision status` IS ONE OF
    `the agency has decided`
    `the agency must decide by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `the period has not started: the information the agency asked for has not been given`
    `taken to be refused (ss 24, 32, 39): the person is entitled to an information notice and may apply for internal review`

-- ss 24(1), 32(1), 39(1): "If the agency fails to decide [it] within the decision-making period, the failure is taken
-- to be a decision by the agency to refuse [it]." (2): the person is entitled to an information notice.
GIVEN `the kind`                                 IS A `Request kind`
      `the day the agency received it`           IS A DATE
      `an information request was made`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the information request`       IS A DATE
      `the information has been given`           IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the information was given`        IS A DATE
      `the days of extension`                    IS A NUMBER
      `the agency has decided`                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `today`                                    IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Decision status`
`the decision status` `the kind` `the day the agency received it` `an information request was made` `the day of the information request` `the information has been given` `the day the information was given` `the days of extension` `the agency has decided` `today` MEANS
    IF `the agency has decided`
    THEN `the agency has decided`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the last day of the decision-making period` `the kind` `the day the agency received it` `an information request was made` `the day of the information request` `the information has been given` `the day the information was given` `the days of extension`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `the period has not started: the information the agency asked for has not been given`
         WHEN JUST `the last day` THEN
            IF `today` `is no later than` `the last day`
            THEN `the agency must decide by` `the last day`
            ELSE `taken to be refused (ss 24, 32, 39): the person is entitled to an information notice and may apply for internal review`

§§ `schedule 1, ss 14, 22, 45-48 -- interim and lifetime participation`

-- Schedule 1: "participation period, for an interim participant, means-- (a) if the participant is a child less than 4
-- years--the period starting the day the participant is accepted into the scheme and ending the day the participant
-- turns 6; or (b) otherwise--the period of 2 years starting the day the participant is accepted into the scheme."
-- "Less than 4 years" is read at the day of acceptance (a READING). The 2 years starting on the day of acceptance end
-- on the day before its second anniversary, counted as 2 years after the day before acceptance, so that a period
-- starting on 29 February ends on 28 February.
GIVEN `the day of birth`    IS A DATE
      `the day accepted`    IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the participation period` `the day of birth` `the day accepted` MEANS
    IF `the day accepted` `is no later than` (`the day` 1 `days before` (`the day` 4 `years after` `the day of birth`))
    THEN `the day` 6 `years after` `the day of birth`
    ELSE `the day` 2 `years after` (`the day` 1 `days before` `the day accepted`)

-- s 45(3): "The agency must give the interim participant notice of the review at least 28 days before carrying out the
-- review."
GIVEN `the day of the review` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for notice of a review (s 45(3))` `the day of the review` MEANS `the day` 28 `days before` `the day of the review`

-- s 47(1): "Within 14 days after making a decision under section 46, the agency must give notice of the decision".
GIVEN `the day of the decision` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for notice of a review decision (s 47(1))` `the day of the decision` MEANS `the day` 14 `days after` `the day of the decision`

DECLARE `End of interim participation` IS ONE OF
    `a lifetime participant from the decision (s 46(4))`
    `participation ends at the end of the participation period, on` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `participation ends on the earlier day stated in the notice (s 46(5)(b))` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `taken to be no longer eligible: participation ends at the end of the participation period (s 48), on` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE

-- s 46(1)-(5): after a review, the agency decides whether the participant is still eligible and, if so, whether it is
-- satisfied the injury will likely continue to meet the eligibility criteria after the period; if both, "The agency
-- must accept the person as a participant ... for the rest of the person's life" (4); otherwise the participant stops
-- "(a) at the end of the participation period; or (b) if the agency decides the participant is no longer eligible
-- ...--on an earlier day stated in the notice". s 48(1): no decision before the end of the period: taken to be no
-- longer eligible, and participation stops at the end of the period. The decisions are the agency's, asked as facts.
GIVEN `the last day of the period`                 IS A DATE
      `a review decision was made before the end`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agency decided the person is still eligible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agency is satisfied the injury will continue to meet the criteria` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states an earlier day`           IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earlier day stated`                     IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `End of interim participation`
`the s 46 answer` `the last day of the period` `a review decision was made before the end` `the agency decided the person is still eligible` `the agency is satisfied the injury will continue to meet the criteria` `the notice states an earlier day` `the earlier day stated` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a review decision was made before the end`
            THEN `taken to be no longer eligible: participation ends at the end of the participation period (s 48), on` `the last day of the period`
        IF `the agency decided the person is still eligible` AND `the agency is satisfied the injury will continue to meet the criteria`
            THEN `a lifetime participant from the decision (s 46(4))`
        IF (NOT `the agency decided the person is still eligible`) AND `the notice states an earlier day` AND `the earlier day stated` `is no later than` `the last day of the period`
            THEN `participation ends on the earlier day stated in the notice (s 46(5)(b))` `the earlier day stated`
        OTHERWISE `participation ends at the end of the participation period, on` `the last day of the period`

§§ `s 9 -- excluded treatment, care and support`

DECLARE `Service facts` HAS
    `provided without charge`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `for a child, within the ordinary costs of raising a child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `personal assistance or community participation attendant care` IS A BOOLEAN
    `prescribed by regulation as needing a registered provider` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provided at a hospital as part of its services`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider is a registered provider`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `part of a medical trial or experimental`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `part of a public sector health service`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `provided by State emergency services`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `prescribed by regulation as excluded`                     IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 9(1): "Excluded treatment, care and support is treatment, care and support that-- (a) is provided without charge;
-- or (b) if the participant is a child--ordinarily falls within the ordinary costs of raising a child; or (c) must be
-- provided by a registered provider but is provided by a person who, at the time of provision, is not a registered
-- provider; or (d) ... a medical trial or ... experimental basis; or (e) ... a public sector health service ...; or (f)
-- ... State emergency services ...; or (g) is prescribed by regulation." (2): attendant care and support services that
-- are personal assistance services or services to help the person take part in the community, and anything else
-- prescribed, "must be provided by a registered provider"; (3): "However, subsection (2)(a) does not apply if the
-- treatment, care and support is being provided ... at a hospital ... as part of the services provided by the
-- hospital." The list in s 9(1) is the definition ("is"), so the answer is a plain yes or no.
GIVEN `s` IS A `Service facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is excluded treatment, care and support (s 9)` `s` IF
        `s`'s `provided without charge`
    OR  `s`'s `for a child, within the ordinary costs of raising a child`
    OR  (`must be provided by a registered provider` AND (NOT (`s`'s `the provider is a registered provider`)))
    OR  `s`'s `part of a medical trial or experimental`
    OR  `s`'s `part of a public sector health service`
    OR  `s`'s `provided by State emergency services`
    OR  `s`'s `prescribed by regulation as excluded`
    WHERE
        `must be provided by a registered provider` MEANS
                (`s`'s `personal assistance or community participation attendant care` AND (NOT (`s`'s `provided at a hospital as part of its services`)))
            OR  `s`'s `prescribed by regulation as needing a registered provider`

§§ `ss 35 and 37 -- payment requests`

-- s 35(3): "A payment request must be made within 6 months after the expense is incurred." (4): "However, the agency
-- may accept a later payment request if the agency considers it is fair and reasonable ..." (2): no payment request
-- for an expense incurred in the period of a funding agreement the person has for that treatment, care or support.
GIVEN `the day the expense was incurred` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for a payment request (s 35(3))` `the day the expense was incurred` MEANS
    `the day` 6 `months after` `the day the expense was incurred`

DECLARE `Payment request timing` IS ONE OF
    `no payment request may be made: the expense falls in the period of my funding agreement (s 35(2))`
    `a payment request may be made, in time, up to` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `late: the agency may accept it only if it considers that fair and reasonable (s 35(4))`

GIVEN `the day the expense was incurred`          IS A DATE
      `a funding agreement covers the expense`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the request`                    IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Payment request timing`
`the s 35 answer` `the day the expense was incurred` `a funding agreement covers the expense` `the day of the request` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a funding agreement covers the expense`
            THEN `no payment request may be made: the expense falls in the period of my funding agreement (s 35(2))`
        IF `the day of the request` `is no later than` (`the last day for a payment request (s 35(3))` `the day the expense was incurred`)
            THEN `a payment request may be made, in time, up to` (`the last day for a payment request (s 35(3))` `the day the expense was incurred`)
        OTHERWISE `late: the agency may accept it only if it considers that fair and reasonable (s 35(4))`

-- s 36(3): "The due day must be at least 10 days after the information request is given." (4): "The payment request
-- lapses if the requested information is not given to the agency-- (a) by the due day; or (b) by a later day agreed
-- ..."
DECLARE `Lapse` IS ONE OF
    `the payment request has not lapsed`
    `the payment request lapses unless the information is given by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `the payment request has lapsed (s 36(4))`
    `the stated due day is earlier than s 36(3) allows; the Act does not say whether the request can lapse`

GIVEN `the day the information request was given` IS A DATE
      `the due day stated`                        IS A DATE
      `a later day was agreed`                    IS A BOOLEAN
      `the later day agreed`                      IS A DATE
      `the information has been given`            IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the information was given`         IS A DATE
      `today`                                     IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Lapse`
`the s 36 answer` `the day the information request was given` `the due day stated` `a later day was agreed` `the later day agreed` `the information has been given` `the day the information was given` `today` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT ((`the day` 10 `days after` `the day the information request was given`) `is no later than` `the due day stated`)
            THEN `the stated due day is earlier than s 36(3) allows; the Act does not say whether the request can lapse`
        IF `the information has been given` AND `the day the information was given` `is no later than` `the last day`
            THEN `the payment request has not lapsed`
        IF `today` `is no later than` `the last day`
            THEN `the payment request lapses unless the information is given by` `the last day`
        OTHERWISE `the payment request has lapsed (s 36(4))`
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS
            IF `a later day was agreed`
            THEN `the later of` `the due day stated` `and` `the later day agreed`
            ELSE `the due day stated`

DECLARE `Payment decision` IS ONE OF
    `the agency must approve, and pay within 28 days after deciding, in Australian dollars,` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the agency may approve or refuse (s 37(1), (3)); if it approves it must pay within 28 days after deciding, in Australian dollars, at most` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the agency need not approve: the expense was not incurred while the person was a participant (s 37(2)(a)); it decides to approve or refuse (s 37(1)); if it approves it must pay within 28 days after deciding, in Australian dollars, at most` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `no payment request lies for an expense incurred during a suspension: the participant is taken not to be a participant for division 3 (ss 35(1), 52(6))`

-- s 37(2): "The agency must approve the payment request if-- (a) the expense is incurred in the period the participant
-- is a participant in the scheme; and (b) the treatment, care or support that the request relates to is an approved
-- service for the participant." (3): it "may approve the payment request even though the treatment, care or support is
-- not an approved service". (4): pay "within 28 days after making the decision". (5): "the agency is not liable to pay a
-- part of the requested amount that exceeds-- (a) [within Australia] an amount prescribed by regulation for the
-- treatment, care or support; or (b) [outside Australia] the average cost of providing the treatment, care or support
-- in Queensland." (6) and schedule 1: an approved service is in the support plan (or, with no plan, a service request
-- approval), and "does not include excluded treatment, care and support, unless" the plan or approval specifically
-- states it. s 52(6): "For part 4, division 3, the participant is taken not to be a participant in the scheme for the
-- period of the suspension"; a payment request lies only for an expense "for the treatment, care or support of a
-- participant" (s 35(1)), so an expense incurred during a suspension is read as giving no payment request (a fork line;
-- the other reading lets the agency approve or refuse under s 37(1)). s 37(3) covers only a service that is not an
-- approved service; for an expense incurred while the person was not a participant, s 37(2) does not bind the agency
-- and s 37(1) leaves it to approve or refuse.
-- The regulation's amounts are not deposited: where one is prescribed it is asked; where none is (or for outside
-- Australia, the Queensland average), the figure given is used.
GIVEN `incurred while a participant`                  IS A BOOLEAN
      `incurred during a suspension`                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `listed in my support plan or a service request approval` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is excluded treatment, care and support`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan or approval specifically states it`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requested amount`                            IS A NUMBER
      `a limit applies`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
      `the limit`                                       IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Payment decision`
`the s 37 answer` `incurred while a participant` `incurred during a suspension` `listed in my support plan or a service request approval` `it is excluded treatment, care and support` `the plan or approval specifically states it` `the requested amount` `a limit applies` `the limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `incurred during a suspension`
            THEN `no payment request lies for an expense incurred during a suspension: the participant is taken not to be a participant for division 3 (ss 35(1), 52(6))`
        IF (NOT `incurred while a participant`)
            THEN `the agency need not approve: the expense was not incurred while the person was a participant (s 37(2)(a)); it decides to approve or refuse (s 37(1)); if it approves it must pay within 28 days after deciding, in Australian dollars, at most` `the payable amount`
        IF `an approved service`
            THEN `the agency must approve, and pay within 28 days after deciding, in Australian dollars,` `the payable amount`
        OTHERWISE `the agency may approve or refuse (s 37(1), (3)); if it approves it must pay within 28 days after deciding, in Australian dollars, at most` `the payable amount`
    WHERE
        `an approved service` MEANS
                `listed in my support plan or a service request approval`
            AND ((NOT `it is excluded treatment, care and support`) OR `the plan or approval specifically states it`)
        `the payable amount` MEANS
            IF `a limit applies` THEN `the smaller of` `the requested amount` `and` `the limit` ELSE `the requested amount`

GIVEN `the day of the decision` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to pay (s 37(4))` `the day of the decision` MEANS `the day` 28 `days after` `the day of the decision`

§§ `chapter 2, part 4, division 4 -- treatment, care and support damages (ss 40-44)`

-- s 41(3): "(a) if the claim is made after the participant is accepted as a lifetime participant--within 14 days after
-- the participant is given, or is entitled to be given, a notice under the Insurance Act, section 39(1) or (2); or (b)
-- if the claim is made before ...--within 14 days after the participant is given notice of the participant's acceptance
-- into the scheme as a lifetime participant." (4): later, "but before a final judgment is given, or a settlement is
-- made, ... if-- (a) the insurer and the agency agree ...; and (b) for a claim that is the subject of a proceeding
-- before a court--the court orders that the notice may be given". s 43(5)(a): after a s 43 order, no preservation
-- notice may be given. s 40: the division applies to a lifetime participant with a claim against an insurer; s 13(5):
-- not to a buy-in participant.
GIVEN `the starting day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the s 41 notice` `the starting day` MEANS `the day` 14 `days after` `the starting day`

DECLARE `Preservation notice` IS ONE OF
    `division 4 does not apply: not a lifetime participant with a claim against an insurer (s 40, s 13(5))`
    `no: a court has ordered under s 43 that I may not be awarded treatment, care and support damages (s 43(5))`
    `I must give the s 41 notice to the agency and the insurer by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `late: a final judgment has been given or a settlement made, so the notice can no longer be given (s 41(4))`
    `late: the notice may still be given, because the insurer and the agency agree (and any court has so ordered) (s 41(4))`
    `late: the notice may be given only if the insurer and the agency agree and, if the claim is in court, the court orders it (s 41(4))`

GIVEN `a lifetime participant with a claim against an insurer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a s 43 order has been made`                IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim was made after acceptance as a lifetime participant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the Insurance Act s 39 notice`  IS A DATE
      `the day of the notice of lifetime acceptance` IS A DATE
      `today`                                     IS A DATE
      `a final judgment or settlement has happened` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insurer and the agency agree`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is in court`                     IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has ordered that it may be given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Preservation notice`
`the s 41 answer` `a lifetime participant with a claim against an insurer` `a s 43 order has been made` `the claim was made after acceptance as a lifetime participant` `the day of the Insurance Act s 39 notice` `the day of the notice of lifetime acceptance` `today` `a final judgment or settlement has happened` `the insurer and the agency agree` `the claim is in court` `the court has ordered that it may be given` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a lifetime participant with a claim against an insurer`
            THEN `division 4 does not apply: not a lifetime participant with a claim against an insurer (s 40, s 13(5))`
        IF `a s 43 order has been made`
            THEN `no: a court has ordered under s 43 that I may not be awarded treatment, care and support damages (s 43(5))`
        IF `today` `is no later than` `the last day`
            THEN `I must give the s 41 notice to the agency and the insurer by` `the last day`
        IF `a final judgment or settlement has happened`
            THEN `late: a final judgment has been given or a settlement made, so the notice can no longer be given (s 41(4))`
        IF `the insurer and the agency agree` AND ((NOT `the claim is in court`) OR `the court has ordered that it may be given`)
            THEN `late: the notice may still be given, because the insurer and the agency agree (and any court has so ordered) (s 41(4))`
        OTHERWISE `late: the notice may be given only if the insurer and the agency agree and, if the claim is in court, the court orders it (s 41(4))`
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS
            IF `the claim was made after acceptance as a lifetime participant`
            THEN `the last day for the s 41 notice` `the day of the Insurance Act s 39 notice`
            ELSE `the last day for the s 41 notice` `the day of the notice of lifetime acceptance`

DECLARE `Contribution` IS ONE OF
    `the agency is liable to contribute towards the insurer's liability for treatment, care and support damages (s 42(1))`
    `no: no preservation notice has been given (s 42(1))`
    `no longer: contributory negligence reduces my damages by 50% or more (s 42(2)(a))`
    `no longer: a court refused to sanction my preservation notice (s 42(2)(b))`
    `no longer: a court made a s 43 order (s 42(2)(c))`
    `no longer: I withdrew my preservation notice (s 42(2)(d))`

-- s 42(1): "If the participant gives a preservation notice, the agency is liable to contribute towards the insurer's
-- liability, if any, on the claim for treatment, care and support damages." (2): "However, the agency stops being liable
-- to contribute if-- (a) a court decides, or the parties to the claim agree by way of settlement, that-- (i) the
-- participant is guilty of contributory negligence ...; and (ii) the damages ... are to be reduced, because of the
-- contributory negligence, by 50% or more; or (b) a court decides, under section 41(7), not to sanction the
-- preservation notice; or (c) a court makes an order, under section 43 ...; or (d) for a participant other than a
-- participant whose preservation notice has been sanctioned by a court--the participant, by notice to the agency and
-- the insurer, withdraws the preservation notice." s 43(5)(b): after a s 43 order a preservation notice is taken not to
-- have been given; (c) answers that first.
GIVEN `a preservation notice was given`                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `contributory negligence was decided or agreed`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reduction for contributory negligence, percent` IS A NUMBER
      `a court refused to sanction the notice`            IS A BOOLEAN
      `a s 43 order has been made`                        IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court sanctioned the notice`                     IS A BOOLEAN
      `I withdrew the notice`                             IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Contribution`
`the s 42 answer` `a preservation notice was given` `contributory negligence was decided or agreed` `the reduction for contributory negligence, percent` `a court refused to sanction the notice` `a s 43 order has been made` `a court sanctioned the notice` `I withdrew the notice` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a s 43 order has been made`
            THEN `no longer: a court made a s 43 order (s 42(2)(c))`
        IF NOT `a preservation notice was given`
            THEN `no: no preservation notice has been given (s 42(1))`
        IF `contributory negligence was decided or agreed` AND `the reduction for contributory negligence, percent` AT LEAST 50
            THEN `no longer: contributory negligence reduces my damages by 50% or more (s 42(2)(a))`
        IF `a court refused to sanction the notice`
            THEN `no longer: a court refused to sanction my preservation notice (s 42(2)(b))`
        IF `I withdrew the notice` AND (NOT `a court sanctioned the notice`)
            THEN `no longer: I withdrew my preservation notice (s 42(2)(d))`
        OTHERWISE `the agency is liable to contribute towards the insurer's liability for treatment, care and support damages (s 42(1))`

DECLARE `How damages were awarded` IS ONE OF
    `under a settlement or judgment that must be sanctioned by a court or the public trustee`
    `under a binding settlement that needs no sanction`
    `under a final judgment of a court that needs no sanction`

-- s 44(8): "acceptance period means-- (a) if the binding settlement or final judgment ... must ... be sanctioned by a
-- court or the public trustee--the period of 14 days after the sanction is given; or (b) [a settlement] the period of
-- 14 days after the settlement is made; or (c) [a judgment] the period of 14 days after the period for lodging an
-- appeal against the judgment ends." The appeal period is set by the court rules, not this Act: its last day is asked.
GIVEN `how`                   IS A `How damages were awarded`
      `the day of the sanction, settlement, or end of the appeal period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the acceptance period (s 44(8))` `how` `the day of the sanction, settlement, or end of the appeal period` MEANS
    `the day` 14 `days after` `the day of the sanction, settlement, or end of the appeal period`

DECLARE `Acceptance choice` IS ONE OF
    `I accept the awarded damages`
    `I do not accept the awarded damages`
    `I have not yet given notice`

DECLARE `Awarded damages` IS ONE OF
    `s 44 does not apply: the agency is not liable to contribute, or no treatment, care and support damages were awarded`
    `the agency must pay me, in Australian dollars,` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `neither the agency nor the insurer must pay the awarded treatment, care and support damages (s 44(5))`
    `I must tell the agency and the insurer whether I accept, by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `the acceptance period has ended without my notice; the Act does not say what follows`

-- s 44(2): "The participant must, within the acceptance period, give notice to the agency and the insurer stating
-- whether or not the participant accepts the awarded treatment, care and support damages." (3): if accepted, "(a) the
-- agency must pay to the participant the amount of the awarded treatment, care and support damages, less any amount
-- that relates to the period of the participant's participation in the scheme; and (b) the participant stops being a
-- participant in the scheme when the participant receives the payment ...; and (c) ... the insurer is not liable to pay
-- [them] ..." (5): if not accepted, "neither the agency nor the insurer is liable to pay the amount of the awarded
-- treatment, care and support damages". Neither subsection says what follows when no notice is given (a finding).
GIVEN `s 44 applies`                          IS A BOOLEAN
      `the choice`                            IS AN `Acceptance choice`
      `the awarded damages`                   IS A NUMBER
      `the part relating to my participation` IS A NUMBER
      `the last day of the acceptance period` IS A DATE
      `today`                                 IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Awarded damages`
`the s 44 answer` `s 44 applies` `the choice` `the awarded damages` `the part relating to my participation` `the last day of the acceptance period` `today` MEANS
    IF NOT `s 44 applies`
    THEN `s 44 does not apply: the agency is not liable to contribute, or no treatment, care and support damages were awarded`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the choice`
         WHEN `I accept the awarded damages` THEN `the agency must pay me, in Australian dollars,` (`the awarded damages` MINUS `the part relating to my participation`)
         WHEN `I do not accept the awarded damages` THEN `neither the agency nor the insurer must pay the awarded treatment, care and support damages (s 44(5))`
         WHEN `I have not yet given notice` THEN
            IF `today` `is no later than` `the last day of the acceptance period`
            THEN `I must tell the agency and the insurer whether I accept, by` `the last day of the acceptance period`
            ELSE `the acceptance period has ended without my notice; the Act does not say what follows`

§§ `chapter 2, part 6 -- leaving Australia (ss 49-52)`

DECLARE `Absence notice` IS ONE OF
    `no duty under s 50: part 6 does not apply`
    `no duty under s 50: a service request was made, or a funding agreement entered into, for the care abroad before I leave (s 50(3))`
    `I must notify the agency of my absence by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `I gave notice in time`
    `I did not notify in time: an offence (up to 10 penalty units) unless I have a reasonable excuse (s 50(1))`

-- s 49: part 6 applies if "(a) the participant leaves Australia; and (b) while the participant is absent ..., expenses
-- are, or are likely to be, incurred by or for the participant for the participant's treatment, care or support; and
-- (c) the agency did not, in deciding the approved services ..., consider the need for treatment, care and support to
-- be provided outside Australia ..." s 50(1): "At least 1 month before leaving Australia, the participant must give
-- notice of the absence to the agency, unless the participant has a reasonable excuse. Maximum penalty--10 penalty
-- units." (3): not if, before leaving, a service request is made, or a funding agreement entered into, for the care
-- abroad. Whether an excuse is reasonable is for a court, so the answer names it as a condition.
GIVEN `the day of leaving` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to notify of an absence (s 50(1))` `the day of leaving` MEANS `the day` (0 MINUS 1) `months after` `the day of leaving`

GIVEN `part 6 applies`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `a service request or funding agreement covers the care abroad` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of leaving`                               IS A DATE
      `notice was given`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day notice was given`                         IS A DATE
      `today`                                            IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Absence notice`
`the s 50 answer` `part 6 applies` `a service request or funding agreement covers the care abroad` `the day of leaving` `notice was given` `the day notice was given` `today` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `part 6 applies`
            THEN `no duty under s 50: part 6 does not apply`
        IF `a service request or funding agreement covers the care abroad`
            THEN `no duty under s 50: a service request was made, or a funding agreement entered into, for the care abroad before I leave (s 50(3))`
        IF `notice was given` AND `the day notice was given` `is no later than` `the last day`
            THEN `I gave notice in time`
        IF `today` `is no later than` `the last day`
            THEN `I must notify the agency of my absence by` `the last day`
        OTHERWISE `I did not notify in time: an offence (up to 10 penalty units) unless I have a reasonable excuse (s 50(1))`
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS `the last day to notify of an absence (s 50(1))` `the day of leaving`

DECLARE `Claim position` IS ONE OF
    `no claim has been made against an insurer for my injury`
    `a claim was made, and the insurer denied liability or a court held it not liable`
    `a claim was made, and liability has not been denied`

DECLARE `Suspension` IS ONE OF
    `s 52 does not apply to a buy-in participant (s 13(5))`
    `the agency may suspend my participation for all or part of my absence; while suspended I cannot be paid on payment requests (s 52(3), (6))`
    `s 52 gives the agency no power to suspend me on these facts`

-- s 52(1): "The agency may suspend the participant's participation ... if-- (a) the agency is satisfied the participant
-- has left Australia for more than 3 consecutive months; and (b) either of the following applies-- (i) a claim has not
-- been made against an insurer ...; (ii) a claim has been made ..., but the insurer has denied liability on the claim
-- or has been held by a court not to be liable ..." (2): "Also, the agency may suspend ... if the agency considers that
-- the participant's absence from Australia will, or is likely to, adversely affect-- (a) the participant's condition
-- ...; or (b) the participant's prospects of improvement or rehabilitation." "More than 3 consecutive months" is worked
-- out from the day of leaving and the last day of the absence (or the day asked about); the agency's satisfaction is
-- assumed to follow the dates, and its view under (2) is asked as a fact. The answer is the agency's power, never its
-- decision.
GIVEN `a buy-in participant`                 IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of leaving`                   IS A DATE
      `the last day of the absence so far`   IS A DATE
      `the claim position`                   IS A `Claim position`
      `the agency considers the absence will harm my condition or prospects` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Suspension`
`the s 52 answer` `a buy-in participant` `the day of leaving` `the last day of the absence so far` `the claim position` `the agency considers the absence will harm my condition or prospects` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a buy-in participant`
            THEN `s 52 does not apply to a buy-in participant (s 13(5))`
        IF (`more than 3 consecutive months` AND (NOT (`the claim position` EQUALS `a claim was made, and liability has not been denied`)))
                OR `the agency considers the absence will harm my condition or prospects`
            THEN `the agency may suspend my participation for all or part of my absence; while suspended I cannot be paid on payment requests (s 52(3), (6))`
        OTHERWISE `s 52 gives the agency no power to suspend me on these facts`
    WHERE
        `more than 3 consecutive months` MEANS
            `the last day of the absence so far` `is after` (`the day` 3 `months after` `the day of leaving`)

§§ `s 53 -- telling the agency about a claim`

DECLARE `Claim notice` IS ONE OF
    `no duty under s 53`
    `I must tell the agency about the claim by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `I told the agency in time`
    `I did not tell the agency in time: an offence, up to 10 penalty units (s 53(2))`

-- s 53(1): "This section applies if-- (a) a person makes an application in relation to a serious personal injury and,
-- before the application is decided, a claim is made for the injury; or (b) a person makes a claim for a participant's
-- injury after the participant is accepted into the scheme." (2): "Within 14 days of making the claim, the person must
-- give the agency notice stating-- (a) that the person has made the claim; and (b) the day the claim was made; and (c)
-- the insurer against whom the claim has been made. Maximum penalty--10 penalty units." No excuse is given in the text.
GIVEN `the day of the claim` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to tell the agency of a claim (s 53(2))` `the day of the claim` MEANS `the day` 14 `days after` `the day of the claim`

GIVEN `s 53 applies`               IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the claim`       IS A DATE
      `notice was given`           IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day notice was given`   IS A DATE
      `today`                      IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Claim notice`
`the s 53 answer` `s 53 applies` `the day of the claim` `notice was given` `the day notice was given` `today` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `s 53 applies`
            THEN `no duty under s 53`
        IF `notice was given` AND `the day notice was given` `is no later than` `the last day`
            THEN `I told the agency in time`
        IF `today` `is no later than` `the last day`
            THEN `I must tell the agency about the claim by` `the last day`
        OTHERWISE `I did not tell the agency in time: an offence, up to 10 penalty units (s 53(2))`
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS `the last day to tell the agency of a claim (s 53(2))` `the day of the claim`

§§ `chapter 6 -- reviews`

DECLARE `Internal review timing` IS ONE OF
    `I may apply for internal review up to` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `the 28 days have not started: I was not given the information notice; I may ask for one (s 106(2)-(3))`
    `late: only if the agency extends the time (s 107(2))`

-- s 106(1): a person "given, or ... entitled to be given, an information notice" may apply for internal review. s
-- 107(1)(b)(ii): if given an information notice, the application must "be made within 28 days after the applicant is
-- given the information notice". (2): "However, the agency may, at any time, extend the time". s 105: no QCAT review
-- without internal review first.
GIVEN `I was given the information notice`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I was given it`               IS A DATE
      `the day of the application`           IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Internal review timing`
`the s 107 answer` `I was given the information notice` `the day I was given it` `the day of the application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `I was given the information notice`
            THEN `the 28 days have not started: I was not given the information notice; I may ask for one (s 106(2)-(3))`
        IF `the day of the application` `is no later than` (`the day` 28 `days after` `the day I was given it`)
            THEN `I may apply for internal review up to` (`the day` 28 `days after` `the day I was given it`)
        OTHERWISE `late: only if the agency extends the time (s 107(2))`

-- s 109(7): "decision period means-- (a) if an information request for the internal review application is made--the
-- period of 28 days after the further information requested is given to the agency; or (b) otherwise--the period of 28
-- days after the agency receives the internal review application." (4): no decision within it: "the agency is taken to
-- have made an internal review decision confirming the original decision". s 108(2): an information request must be
-- made within 28 days after the application is received (one made later is read as no information request, as above).
-- s 110(1): notice of the decision within 14 days after making it; (3): no notice, the decision is taken to be
-- confirmed.
DECLARE `Internal review status` IS ONE OF
    `the agency has made its internal review decision`
    `the agency must decide the internal review by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `the period has not started: the information the agency asked for has not been given`
    `taken to confirm the original decision (s 109(4)); I am entitled to a decision notice (s 110(4))`

GIVEN `the day the agency received the application` IS A DATE
      `an information request was made`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the information request`          IS A DATE
      `the information has been given`              IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the information was given`           IS A DATE
      `the agency has decided`                      IS A BOOLEAN
      `today`                                       IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Internal review status`
`the s 109 answer` `the day the agency received the application` `an information request was made` `the day of the information request` `the information has been given` `the day the information was given` `the agency has decided` `today` MEANS
    IF `the agency has decided`
    THEN `the agency has made its internal review decision`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the last day of the decision-making period` `a service request (ss 28, 31)` `the day the agency received the application` `an information request was made` `the day of the information request` `the information has been given` `the day the information was given` 0
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `the period has not started: the information the agency asked for has not been given`
         WHEN JUST `the last day` THEN
            IF `today` `is no later than` `the last day`
            THEN `the agency must decide the internal review by` `the last day`
            ELSE `taken to confirm the original decision (s 109(4)); I am entitled to a decision notice (s 110(4))`

DECLARE `Medical matter` IS ONE OF
    `whether the motor accident is the medical cause of the serious personal injury`
    `whether the injury meets the eligibility criteria, on matters of a medical nature`
    `whether an interim participant's injury will likely continue to meet the eligibility criteria, on matters of a medical nature`
    `another matter of a medical nature prescribed by regulation`
    `a matter that is not a medical matter`

DECLARE `Medical tribunal referral` IS ONE OF
    `no: the decision involves no medical matter (s 112(1)); review is by QCAT`
    `I may ask the agency to refer the medical matter to a medical tribunal up to` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `no: the 28 days for a referral request have ended (s 112(3))`

-- s 112(1)-(3): for a decision on a "medical matter", a person given (or entitled to be given) a decision notice may
-- ask the agency to refer the matter to a medical tribunal; "The referral request must be made within 28 days after
-- the decision notice is given, or required to be given, to the person." s 113(1): the agency then must refer it.
-- The text gives no power to extend the 28 days, so a late request answers no (a fork line).
GIVEN `the matter`                                IS A `Medical matter`
      `the day the decision notice was given or required` IS A DATE
      `the day of the request`                    IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Medical tribunal referral`
`the s 112 answer` `the matter` `the day the decision notice was given or required` `the day of the request` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the matter` EQUALS `a matter that is not a medical matter`
            THEN `no: the decision involves no medical matter (s 112(1)); review is by QCAT`
        IF `the day of the request` `is no later than` (`the day` 28 `days after` `the day the decision notice was given or required`)
            THEN `I may ask the agency to refer the medical matter to a medical tribunal up to` (`the day` 28 `days after` `the day the decision notice was given or required`)
        OTHERWISE `no: the 28 days for a referral request have ended (s 112(3))`

-- s 118(3): "At least 10 business days before the injured person is scheduled to attend before the tribunal, the
-- injured person must give the tribunal and the agency a copy of any relevant document the injured person wants
-- considered by the tribunal." (6): the tribunal cannot rely on a document not exchanged under the subdivision, except
-- a doctor's report it arranged or a medical image the injured person gives (7).
GIVEN `the day of attendance` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays`   IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to give documents to the medical tribunal (s 118(3))` `the day of attendance` `the public holidays` MEANS
    `the business day` 10 `business days before` `the day of attendance` `the public holidays`

DECLARE `QCAT timing` IS ONE OF
    `no: I must first apply for internal review (s 105)`
    `the medical tribunal's decision on the medical matter is final and not reviewable by QCAT (s 123); QCAT may review the rest of the decision, applying up to` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `I may apply to QCAT within the time the QCAT Act sets (not deposited)`

-- s 105: "A person may not apply to QCAT for review of a decision unless the person has applied for an internal review
-- of the decision". s 127(1): QCAT reviews the internal review decision "as provided under the QCAT Act" (the time is
-- the QCAT Act's, not deposited). (2)-(3): where a medical matter was referred to a medical tribunal, the application
-- "may be made within 28 days after the medical tribunal gives notice, under section 124, of its decision". s 123: the
-- tribunal's decision on the medical matter "is final and is not reviewable by QCAT".
GIVEN `I applied for internal review`            IS A BOOLEAN
      `a medical matter was referred to a medical tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the tribunal's notice`        IS A DATE
GIVETH A `QCAT timing`
`the s 127 answer` `I applied for internal review` `a medical matter was referred to a medical tribunal` `the day of the tribunal's notice` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `I applied for internal review`
            THEN `no: I must first apply for internal review (s 105)`
        IF `a medical matter was referred to a medical tribunal`
            THEN `the medical tribunal's decision on the medical matter is final and not reviewable by QCAT (s 123); QCAT may review the rest of the decision, applying up to` (`the day` 28 `days after` `the day of the tribunal's notice`)
        OTHERWISE `I may apply to QCAT within the time the QCAT Act sets (not deposited)`

§§ `chapter 8 -- offences`

DECLARE `Offence` IS ONE OF
    `not notifying the agency before leaving Australia (s 50)`
    `not telling the agency about a claim within 14 days (s 53)`
    `defrauding or deliberately misleading the agency (s 132)`
    `giving the agency information I know is false or misleading (s 133)`

DECLARE `Maximum penalty` HAS
    `penalty units`           IS A NUMBER
    `months of imprisonment`  IS A NUMBER

-- The "Maximum penalty" lines of ss 50(1), 53(2), 132(1) and 133(1). (s 131(4) binds an entity given personal
-- information by the agency, not the injured person, and is left out.) The dollar value of a penalty unit is set
-- by the Penalties and Sentences Regulation 2015 (not deposited), so the answer is in penalty units.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence`
GIVETH A `Maximum penalty`
`the maximum penalty` `the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `not notifying the agency before leaving Australia (s 50)` THEN `Maximum penalty` WITH `penalty units` IS 10, `months of imprisonment` IS 0
    WHEN `not telling the agency about a claim within 14 days (s 53)` THEN `Maximum penalty` WITH `penalty units` IS 10, `months of imprisonment` IS 0
    WHEN `defrauding or deliberately misleading the agency (s 132)` THEN `Maximum penalty` WITH `penalty units` IS 400, `months of imprisonment` IS 18
    WHEN `giving the agency information I know is false or misleading (s 133)` THEN `Maximum penalty` WITH `penalty units` IS 150, `months of imprisonment` IS 12

-- s 133(2): "Subsection (1) does not apply to a person if the person, when giving information in a document-- (a) tells
-- the agency, to the best of the person's ability, how the document is false or misleading; and (b) if the person has,
-- or can reasonably obtain, the correct information--gives the correct information." The exception covers information
-- in a document only; for information given otherwise it does not arise (JUST FALSE: "if").
GIVEN `the information was in a document`         IS A BOOLEAN
      `I told the agency how it is false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have or can reasonably get the correct information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I gave the correct information`            IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 133(1) does not apply (s 133(2))` `the information was in a document` `I told the agency how it is false or misleading` `I have or can reasonably get the correct information` `I gave the correct information` IF
        `the information was in a document`
    AND `I told the agency how it is false or misleading`
    AND ((NOT `I have or can reasonably get the correct information`) OR `I gave the correct information`)

-- s 134(2): "A proceeding for the offence must start within-- (a) 1 year after the commission of the offence; or (b) 6
-- months after the offence comes to the complainant's knowledge, but within 2 years after the commission of the
-- offence." Read as: the later of (a) and (b), and (b) never beyond 2 years.
GIVEN `the day of the offence`                    IS A DATE
      `the day it came to the complainant's knowledge` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to start a prosecution (s 134(2))` `the day of the offence` `the day it came to the complainant's knowledge` MEANS
    `the later of` (`the day` 1 `years after` `the day of the offence`)
        `and` (`the earlier of` (`the day` 6 `months after` `the day it came to the complainant's knowledge`) `and` (`the day` 2 `years after` `the day of the offence`))

§ `Regulative rules`

DECLARE `NIIS party` IS ONE OF
    `the participant`
    `the injured person`
    `the agency`

DECLARE `NIIS act` IS ONE OF
    `pay the buy-in contribution`
    `give the s 41 notice`
    `give the s 41 notice late, with the insurer's and the agency's agreement`
    `give notice accepting or not accepting the awarded damages`
    `give notice of the absence`
    `give notice of the claim`
    `decide the application`
    `pay the requested amount`
    `give the documents to the medical tribunal`

-- s 13(3)-(4). Day 0: the day the person is accepted as a buy-in participant. Not paying is no offence: the person
-- stops being a participant and is taken never to have been one.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `NIIS party` `NIIS act`
DECIDE `s 13 -- the buy-in participant must pay the contribution within 28 days` IS
    PARTY `the participant`
    MUST  `pay the buy-in contribution`
    WITHIN 28
    LEST  BREACH BY `the participant` BECAUSE "s 13(4): the contribution was not paid within 28 days after acceptance, so the person stops being a participant and is taken never to have been one"

-- s 41(1), (3)-(4). Day 0: the day the 14 days start from. After 14 days, the notice may still be given with the
-- insurer's and the agency's agreement (and a court order if the claim is in court), up to a final judgment or
-- settlement; that is a permission, so the lapse of the 14 days is no breach.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `NIIS party` `NIIS act`
DECIDE `s 41 -- the participant must give the preservation notice within 14 days, or later only with agreement` IS
    PARTY `the participant`
    MUST  `give the s 41 notice`
    WITHIN 14
    LEST  `the late route`
    WHERE
        `the late route` MEANS
            PARTY `the participant`
            MAY   `give the s 41 notice late, with the insurer's and the agency's agreement`

-- s 44(2). Day 0: the day the acceptance period starts from (the sanction, the settlement, or the end of the appeal
-- period). The Act sets no consequence for silence (finding 6); the breach reason says so.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `NIIS party` `NIIS act`
DECIDE `s 44 -- the participant must say within 14 days whether they accept the awarded damages` IS
    PARTY `the participant`
    MUST  `give notice accepting or not accepting the awarded damages`
    WITHIN 14
    LEST  BREACH BY `the participant` BECAUSE "s 44(2): no notice within the acceptance period; the Act does not say what then happens to the awarded treatment, care and support damages"

-- s 50(1). Day 0: the day the participant decides to travel; the rule runs to the last day a notice can be given,
-- 1 month before leaving.
GIVEN `days to the last day for notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `NIIS party` `NIIS act`
DECIDE `s 50 -- the participant must give notice at least 1 month before leaving Australia` IS
    PARTY `the participant`
    MUST  `give notice of the absence`
    WITHIN `days to the last day for notice`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the participant` BECAUSE "s 50(1): notice of the absence was not given at least 1 month before leaving Australia; an offence (up to 10 penalty units) unless the participant has a reasonable excuse"

-- s 53(2). Day 0: the day the claim is made.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `NIIS party` `NIIS act`
DECIDE `s 53 -- the injured person must tell the agency of a claim within 14 days` IS
    PARTY `the injured person`
    MUST  `give notice of the claim`
    WITHIN 14
    LEST  BREACH BY `the injured person` BECAUSE "s 53(2): the agency was not told of the claim within 14 days of making it; an offence, up to 10 penalty units"

-- ss 22(7), 24. Day 0: the day the decision-making period starts. Missing it is taken to be a refusal, which the person
-- may have reviewed; the breach marks that deemed refusal.
GIVEN `days in the decision-making period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `NIIS party` `NIIS act`
DECIDE `s 22 -- the agency must decide the application within the decision-making period` IS
    PARTY `the agency`
    MUST  `decide the application`
    WITHIN `days in the decision-making period`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the agency` BECAUSE "s 24(1): the application was not decided within the decision-making period, so it is taken to be refused; the applicant is entitled to an information notice and may apply for internal review"

-- s 37(4). Day 0: the day the agency approves the payment request.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `NIIS party` `NIIS act`
DECIDE `s 37 -- the agency must pay an approved payment request within 28 days` IS
    PARTY `the agency`
    MUST  `pay the requested amount`
    WITHIN 28
    LEST  BREACH BY `the agency` BECAUSE "s 37(4): the approved amount was not paid within 28 days after the decision"

-- s 118(3). Day 0: the day the attendance is scheduled from; the rule runs to the 10th business day before it. The
-- consequence of missing it is that the tribunal cannot consider the document (s 118(6)), unless it is a medical image.
GIVEN `days to the last day for documents` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `NIIS party` `NIIS act`
DECIDE `s 118 -- the injured person must give documents at least 10 business days before attending the medical tribunal` IS
    PARTY `the injured person`
    MUST  `give the documents to the medical tribunal`
    WITHIN `days to the last day for documents`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the injured person` BECAUSE "s 118(3), (6): the documents were not given at least 10 business days before the attendance, so the tribunal cannot consider or rely on them (a medical image excepted, s 118(7)(b))"
